    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0841" n="1675" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/731</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-13T10:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 13, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 14, 2.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1234. Referring to the Embassy’s telegram 1206, April 5, 7 p.m., for War Trade
                    Board, No. 14 from Chadbourne.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d722-f1"/> Not having yet
                    secured single permit to export to A[merican] E[xpeditionary] F[orces] under
                    terms of commercial agreement March 7, Embassy ventures to request authority to
                    inform Minister of Foreign Affairs, that Board will grant no more licenses to
                    export trade to Spain, until Spanish Government shall have granted permits to
                    export to <pb facs="0842" n="1676" xml:id="pg1676"/> A.E.F. those articles
                    covered by agreement of March 7 for which application has already been made and
                    to suggest that Spanish Ambassador at Washington be similarly informed. Embassy
                    ventures further to suggest authority to remind Foreign Office that Board is
                    free after May 7 to impose such bunker regulations as it may see fit on Spanish
                    vessels in American waters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
